---
title: Server SDK · activation and the control channel
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant rt as Prepared-environment runtime
  participant sdk as Server SDK
  participant cp as Control plane
  participant ing as Telemetry ingestion

  rt->>sdk: claim-time restart · bootstrap credential + trust anchor
  Note over sdk: Preload, before application code.<br/>Mints server_stream_id and service.instance.id.
  sdk->>cp: open WS /v1/server-sdk/control · bearer bootstrap credential
  sdk->>cp: activation frame · same credential + stream identity
  Note over cp: One activation per stream.<br/>Manifest from the release the Product Signal pinned.
  cp-->>sdk: activation record · signed manifest, credential, endpoint, limits, probe, entry token
  Note over sdk: Verifies the manifest signature, or refuses to instrument.<br/>Installs the sole provider and the manifest's instrumentation.
  loop While active
    sdk->>ing: OTLP/HTTP batch · service-instance credential
    ing-->>sdk: full success
  end
  loop Ahead of each credential expiry
    sdk->>cp: rotate
    cp-->>sdk: fresh short-lived service-instance credential
  end
  loop Each health interval
    sdk->>cp: health report
    Note over cp: Durable record, then a fresh readiness evaluation.
  end
  opt Pause or resume
    cp->>sdk: pause or resume
  end
  opt Termination
    cp->>sdk: terminate
    sdk->>ing: bounded flush
    sdk->>cp: terminal stream report
  end
  Note over sdk,cp: A dropped control connection reconnects with the same bootstrap credential, then rotates.<br/>A restarted process presents a new stream and becomes a new activation.
